From: NixOS for nabu
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8150: keep the speaker amplifiers' default DAI format

sm8150_snd_startup() configures the Speaker Playback link
(QUATERNARY_TDM_RX_0) with a codec DAI format of NB_NF|DSP_A.  It
applies that format to the first codec of the link only, because the
helper call is snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0); on nabu that is
cs35l41_br, while the remaining three amplifiers were never touched.

For cs35l41, DSP_A means "clear CS35L41_ASP_FMT" (cs35l41_set_dai_fmt()
leaves daifmt at 0 for SND_SOC_DAIFMT_DSP_A), which moves SP_FORMAT from
its default 0x18180200 (ASP_FMT = 2, I2S framing; see the reg_defaults
in cs35l41-lib.c) to 0x18180000.

Exactly that first amplifier is the one reported silent on nabu while
the other three play.  The forced DSP_A format is therefore the only
software difference between the working and the silent amplifier, and
the three working ones stay on the power-on default (I2S), which
matches the AFE TDM port (see the qcom,tdm-* sync options in the
q6afedai node).

Stop overriding the amplifier DAI format so that all four CS35L41s stay
on their power-on default.  The CPU DAI format (fmt) is still
configured as before.

Hardware check that confirms/refutes the reasoning: read SP_FORMAT
(register 0x00004808, 4-byte big-endian address and value, i2c7,
addresses 0x40..0x43) on all four amplifiers while audio plays - before
this patch the first one reads back without the ASP_FMT bits set.

Signed-off-by: NixOS for nabu

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -298,23 +298,26 @@
 static int sm8150_snd_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 {
 	unsigned int fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC;
-	unsigned int codec_dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC;
 	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = snd_soc_substream_to_rtd(substream);
 	struct snd_soc_card *card = rtd->card;
 	struct sm8150_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
 	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
-	struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0);
 
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case QUATERNARY_TDM_RX_0:
-		codec_dai_fmt |= SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_DSP_A;
 		if (++(data->quat_tdm_clk_count) == 1) {
 			snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai,
 				Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUAD_TDM_IBIT,
 				12288000, SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK);
 		}
 		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(cpu_dai, fmt);
-		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(codec_dai, codec_dai_fmt);
+		/*
+		 * Leave the amplifier DAI format at its default ASP format
+		 * (I2S): the three amplifiers that play were never touched by
+		 * this code, while the DSP_A format that used to be forced here
+		 * (and only on the first codec of the link) cleared ASP_FMT and
+		 * silenced exactly that amplifier (cs35l41_br on nabu).
+		 */
 		break;
 	case SLIMBUS_0_RX...SLIMBUS_6_TX:
 		break;
